  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Green Story</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Green Story&#x2019;s vision is to get every consumer on the planet ask: &#x201c;What&#x2019;s the impact of my purchase?&#x201d;. Our mission is to make the sustainability information interesting, relevant and personal for every consumer. To that end, they are working to develop the world&#x2019;s most sustainable consumer marketplace. The proposed Marketplace will only sell carbon and water neutral products with fully transparent supply chain information. It will allow more and more companies to sell sustainable products thus creating more choice for consumers.With the support of DGGFTA Green Story seeks to: a) sharply reduce its onboarding costs by automating the footprint calculation. Currently, it takes between 1 to 3 days to manually calculate a product&#x2019;s footprint. Automating this will reduce the footprint calculation time to couple of hours. This will be critical for marketplace where we plan to onboard hundreds of brands/companies each month. Developing this capability will also result in a direct financial contribution from brands of up to $2 million over next 3 years to offset projects in developing countries.  b) expand their market reach by targeting bigger brands who want to offset their residual footprint and showcase supply chain transparency. Supply chain transparency is also critical for the marketplace as consumers want to ensure that sustainability is upheld across the entire supply chain. In addition, showcasing transparency will lead to improving supply chain sustainability at every stage of the product&#x2019;s lifecycle.</narrative>
  </description>
